  "body": "Rung 2 of #31 (M13.3): `camcraft-ui` now builds **and links** for `wasm32-unknown-unknown`. `web/build-app-wasm.sh` produces `camcraft-ui.wasm` next to rung 1's `camcraft-cli.wasm`. This is a partial step (`Refs #31`). The UI does not run in a browser yet.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Shell split (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/`).** `shell.rs` was 1676 lines. It is split three ways:\n  - `shell_window.rs` (native-only, 381 lines): the winit event loop, `Shell` struct, window and surface, GPU bring-up, native refusal dialog and the redraw timing helpers.\n  - `shell_window/frame.rs` (native-only, 409 lines): the per-frame draw and the winit `ApplicationHandler`.\n  - `shell.rs` (923 lines, every target): what any shell shares - `shell_layout`, the dock tabs, the viewport panel, the sim readouts and the headless proof.\n\n  The moved code is unchanged apart from imports and visibility. `VIEW3D_FORMAT` and `Tab::title` became `pub(crate)`. `gpu_init`, `frame_watch` and `os_quit` are also `cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\"))`. On wasm32, `egui_app::run` refuses the windowed entry by name (exit 2) rather than pretending.\n- **`crates/ui/src/file_dialog.rs` (new).** All 13 `rfd::FileDialog` sites (`state.rs`, `state_per_op.rs`, `state_setup_post_options.rs`, `state_tool_library.rs`) now go through one `FileDialog` seam with the same builder API. Native builds forward to rfd unchanged. On wasm32 the seam answers `None` (cancelled) and prints a stderr line naming #31.\n- **`crates/app/src/clock.rs` (new).** `camcraft_app::clock::Instant` is `std::time::Instant` natively and `web_time::Instant` on wasm32, where std's `Instant::now()` panics. It is used at app's 6 timing sites and ui's `state.rs` / `frame_watch.rs`. In geometry, `slice.rs` now reads the clock only while projection profiling is switched on (an environment variable, which a browser can never set), so no new dependency is needed there.\n- **`crates/ui/src/lib.rs`.** `#![cfg_attr(target_arch = \"wasm32\", allow(dead_code))]`. Nothing calls the shared shell on wasm32 until the web runner lands, which would otherwise give 543 dead-code warnings. Native builds keep the lint.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/31-wasm-ui-shell.md`.\n\n## Dependency / script / workflow changes (needs-maintainer)\n\n- `Cargo.toml` [workspace.dependencies]: `web-time = \"1.1\"`. **No new crate enters the tree.** web-time 1.1.0 was already in `Cargo.lock` through winit/egui. The lock diff is one line (camcraft-app's dependency list). License MIT OR Apache-2.0, pure Rust.\n- `crates/app/Cargo.toml`: `web-time` added as a **wasm32-only** target dependency. Native builds do not compile it for app.\n- `crates/ui/Cargo.toml`: `egui-winit` and `rfd` moved to `[target.'cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\"))'.dependencies]`. Native builds are unchanged; wasm32 drops them (egui-winit 0.36.2 does not compile there).\n- `web/build-app-wasm.sh`: a new step 4 builds and links `camcraft-ui.wasm` with the same flecs patch and checks that the file exists.\n- `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: **comment only** on the existing `wasm` job, which runs the script. Triggers are unchanged (`workflow_dispatch` only).\n\n## How it was proved\n\n- **wasm32, recorded local run** (Windows, Git Bash, clang 21 from msys2, wasi-sysroot 34): `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<worktree>/target bash web/build-app-wasm.sh` exited 0 and printed:\n  - `build-app-wasm: linked .../wasm32-unknown-unknown/debug/camcraft-cli.wasm` (rung 1, still links)\n  - `build-app-wasm: linked .../wasm32-unknown-unknown/debug/camcraft-ui.wasm` (rung 2, about 576 MB debug, the whole UI crate incl. egui, egui_dock, egui-wgpu/wgpu, viewport and app)\n\n  No camcraft-ui warnings on wasm32. The tracked `Cargo.lock` was restored afterwards.\n- **Native:** `cargo check -p camcraft-ui --all-targets` is clean. The quick gate was `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`, which fell back to batch because of the Cargo and geometry changes. Results: **all 9 steps ok, 0 failed (37.2 min)** - geometry, cl, tools, post, sim, motion, app, ui (cwd crates/ui) suites and `clippy -D warnings` on all eight crates.\n- **Pinning tests (native):**\n  - `file_dialog::tests::file_dialog_builder_keeps_every_setting`: the seam keeps title, filters, directory and file name.\n  - `clock::tests::clock_seam_is_monotonic_and_does_duration_math`: the alias does the Duration maths `logging::elapsed_ms` and the play worker rely on.\n  - The existing `redraw_tests` moved with their code to `shell_window` and still run. The `#[test]` count is unchanged apart from the two new tests.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- **No in-browser run.** I have no browser here. `camcraft-ui.wasm` links, but it has not been instantiated, and on wasm32 its entry only refuses the windowed path. Running it needs the pieces still owed below.\n- The wasm32 halves of `file_dialog` (returns None) and `clock` (web_time) are type-checked and linked, not executed.\n- The native GUI was not launched (by rule). The windowed code moved verbatim and is covered by compile, clippy and the ui suites.\n\n## Still owed on #31\n\n1. A browser runner: eframe's web runner or the egui web glue, calling `shell::shell_layout`. Remove the wasm32 `allow(dead_code)` when it lands.\n2. Async GPU bring-up in place of the `pollster::block_on` sites (`egui_app/gpu.rs`, `trace.rs`, `trace/composite.rs`, `headless_gpu.rs`).\n3. An async file picker (rfd `AsyncFileDialog` or `<input type=file>`) behind `file_dialog`, with a pending-result slot in `State`.\n4. Run-inline fallbacks where `std::thread::spawn` is used (generate, job, stock_play_worker, state, cpu_eye).\n5. The JS shim for the wasi imports, wasm-bindgen CLI 0.2.129, the page, and the in-browser CI job.\n6. `shell.rs` is still 923 lines, down from 1676. The viewport panel (about 460 lines) is the next seam to split out.\n\nChangelog: camcraft-ui now builds and links for wasm32 (browser shell still owed): native window split from the shared shell, file-dialog and clock seams (#31, PR #841)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nRefs #31\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
